OS - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

The standard os functions (clock, date, time,
difftime; see LUA.md) plus:

os.sleep([seconds])

Waits; other threads keep running and no signals
are lost (every thread sees every signal).
os.sleep(0) waits one tick. Errors with
interrupted on Ctrl+C.

os.getenv([name]) -> value

An environment variable of the current process
(inherited from its parent), or all of them as a
table without a name. PWD is the working
directory.

os.setenv(name, value) -> value

Sets an environment variable of the current
process (nil removes it). Setting PWD changes the
working directory.

os.exit([code])

Ends the running program. The shell treats 0, true
or nothing as success.

os.remove(path) -> boolean

Removes a file or directory (filesystem.remove).

os.rename(from, to) -> boolean

Moves or renames (filesystem.rename).

os.tmpname() -> string

A path in /tmp that doesn't exist yet.

os.execute([command]) -> boolean, code

Runs a shell command line and waits for it.

os.hostname() -> string

This computer's name: $HOSTNAME, else
/etc/hostname, else the first 8 characters of its
address.
